# The pinned benchctl measurement binary, resolved by tools/fetch-benchd.sh
# against ./benchd.pin. A FETCHED ARTIFACT, never repository content: the pin
# (branch/commit/sha256/bytes) is what is reviewed and committed, and the bytes
# are re-verified on every resolve, so committing them here would add a 2 MB
# blob to the history that carries no authority the pin does not already carry.
/benchd-bin/

# Build artifacts
*.so
build/
dist/
.build/
.build-worker/
.build-ci/
# CI tees `swift build` here for tools/ci-swift-warning-gate.sh to read.
swift-build.log
# CI tees tools/test-submission-security.sh here so the non-vacuity floor can be
# re-checked against its printed trailer from outside the suite file.
submission-security.log
.tools/
.mlxfast-cache/
.mlxfast-private/
.cache/

# Reference weights are large and downloaded by setup.sh
reference_weights/*
!reference_weights/.gitkeep

# Participant transformed weights are gitignored by default; opt in if needed
#
# NO .gitkeep HERE, unlike reference_weights/ above. The transform publishes
# weights/ by ATOMIC DIRECTORY REPLACEMENT -- it fills a sibling staging
# directory and then replaceItemAt()s the whole thing into place
# (Sources/MLXFastTransform/Transform.swift) -- so nothing checked in UNDER
# weights/ can survive the documented `mlxfast-swift transform --output weights`
# step. A tracked weights/.gitkeep therefore came back as a deletion in
# `git status` after every documented setup, which is a dirty tree no
# participant can clean without re-adding a file the next transform deletes
# again. reference_weights/ keeps its .gitkeep because it is filled file by
# file by a downloader that never replaces the directory.
#
# The directory does not need to pre-exist: the transform creates it, and
# weights/ is not a benchmark.json editablePaths entry, so the submission
# archiver never looks for it on disk. The harness's tolerance of a stray
# .gitkeep inside weights/ (ignoredRelativePaths in the runtime benchmark and
# TransformVerification) is unaffected and stays correct for anyone who puts
# one back by hand.
weights/*

# The DFlash drafter staged by setup-gemma4-dflash.sh (~860 MB, organizer-pinned
# and downloaded, never authored here) -- a FETCHED ARTIFACT, the same reason
# /benchd-bin/ is ignored above: the pin (repo/revision + the sha256/size
# records in fixtures/gemma4_dflash_drafter.sha256) is what is reviewed and
# committed, it is re-verified on every stage, and committing the bytes would
# add 859 MB to the history that carries no authority the pin does not.
#
# NOT a blanket ban on content here. dflash-head/ is an `optionalEditablePaths`
# entry -- the twin of mtp-head/ -- so a participant MAY declare an in-branch
# drafter (`"source": "in_branch"` in spec-decoder-head.manifest.json) and add it
# with `git add -f`. And dflash-head/README.md is CHECKED IN on purpose: the
# submission archiver fails on an editablePaths entry that is absent on disk,
# so the README keeps the directory present while shipping no weights. Ignore
# the directory's CONTENTS and re-include that one file. The blunter
# `dflash-head/` cannot express this: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a `!dflash-head/README.md` negation under it never takes
# effect and the checked-in README is reported ignored.
dflash-head/*
!dflash-head/README.md

# The assistant (MTP) head staged by setup-gemma4-assistant.sh (~256 MB), for
# every reason the dflash-head block above gives -- the two directories are
# declared twins in benchmark.json (both `editablePaths` AND
# `optionalEditablePaths`, both exempt from the editable-surface byte budget),
# and both are filled by a stager that downloads organizer-pinned bytes and
# verifies them against a checked-in manifest
# (fixtures/gemma4_assistant.sha256). Only dflash-head/ was listed when that
# block landed, so the documented `./setup.sh && ./setup-gemma4-assistant.sh`
# path left ~256 MB of downloaded weights plus setup.sh's own .complete markers
# and .mlxfast-reference-cache.lock sitting in `git status` as untracked files,
# one `git add -A` away from being committed into an editable path. Same shape
# as its twin: ignore the staged CONTENTS, re-include the checked-in README
# that keeps the optional editable path present on disk for `yukon submit`, and
# leave an in-branch head an explicit `git add -f` opt-in.
mtp-head/*
!mtp-head/README.md

# Local results log
results.tsv
m5_artifacts/

# Benchmark contract outputs
score.json
score.json.tmp
# Every local run also writes a checksum sidecar and an integrity record, and
# --local-iterate writes its own score/integrity names (benchmark.sh:112,:190).
# Leaving them untracked-but-not-ignored made the tree permanently dirty, so a
# `git add -A` swept repo-root artifacts into a submission diff -- which
# enforce-modifiable-surface.sh then rejects as outside editablePaths.
score.json.sha256
score.local-*.json
score.local-*.json.sha256
score*.baseline.json
benchmark-integrity.json
benchmark-integrity.local-*.json
correctness_golden.json
correctness_golden*.json
local_correctness_golden.json
private_prompts.json
private_prompts*.json
gpqa_reference_cases.json
gpqa_reference_cases*.json
correctness_prompts/*correctness_golden*.json
correctness_prompts/*golden_prompt*.json
correctness_prompts/*golden_prompt*.txt
correctness_prompts/*private*.json
correctness_prompts/*private*.txt
correctness_prompts/*gpqa_reference_cases*.json

